          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "occurs as a milky juice in several plants, such as the _siphonia cahuca_, called also _hevea guianensis_, _cautschuc_, _jatropha elastica_, _castilleja elastica_, _cecropia pellata_, _ficus religiosa_ and _indica_, _urceolaria elastica_, &c. [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "19th-century trade appellation for natural rubber latex (Hevea spp.); historically grouped with allied tropical latexes such as Gutta Percha.",
