      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Schinken*. DU. *Hammen*. DA. *Skinker*. SW. *Skinkor*. FR. *Jambons*. IT. *Prosciutti*. SP. *Jamones*. PORT. *Presuntas*. RUS. *Okorokü*. POL. *Szynki*,) the thighs of the hog salted and dried. Yorkshire, Hampshire, Wiltshire, and Cumberland, are the counties of England most famous for producing fine hams. The hams of Portugal and Westphalia are exquisitely flavoured; they are frequently imported into Great Britain. We export hams to the West Indies. The Westphalia... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 486]",
