      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_08_Animal_Feeding_Stuff",
      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Hew.* DU. *Hovi.* DA. *Höe.* SW. *Hü.* FR. *Foin.* IT. *Fieno.* SP. *Heno.* PORT. *Feno.* RUS. *Sjeno.* POL. *Siano.* LAT. *Fænum*,) any kind of grass, cut and dried, for the food of cattle. Regulations concerning the hay-market, and the selling of hay and straw, within the bills of mortality and thirty miles of the cities of London and Westminster, are enacted by 36 Geo. 3. c. 88. According to it, no hay or straw shall be sold within the expressed limit, but in... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 494]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
