        "@value": "is dilute alcohol, distilled from the fermented worts of malt or grains. WHITE LEAD, _Carbonate of lead, or Ceruse_. (_Blanc de plomb_, Fr.; _Bleiweiss_, Germ.) This preparation is the only one in general use for painting wood and the plaster walls of apartments white. It mixes well with oil, without having its bright colour impaired, spreads easily under the brush, and gives a uniform coat to wood, stone, metal, &c. It is employed either alone, or with other pigments, to... [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
