      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_42_Fixed_Vegetable_Fats_and_Oils",
      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a greasy liquid; a term applied commercially to two distinct and dissimilar organic products, called fixed or fat oils, and volatile or essential oils. They are further divided into solid butters or fats, and fluid fixed oils. The number of oils now entering into commerce is very large, those of any importance will be found noticed in their alphabetical order. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 276]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
