      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "The total quantity of cotton yarn exported from the United Kingdom in 1874 was 220,682,919 lbs., of the value of 14,517,425*l.*, and the total quantity of cotton piece goods exported in the same year was 5,606,639,044 yards, of the value of 59,730,200*l.*, showing an increase in quantity, but a decrease in value when compared with the two preceding years 1872 and 1873. [J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1698]",
