      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_00_Live_Animals",
      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Ochsen*. DU. *Ossen*. DA. *Oxer*. SW. *Oxar*. FR. *Bœufs*. IT. *Bugl*. SP. *Bucies*. PORT. *Bois*. RUS. *Buki*. POL. *Woly*. LAT. *Boves*.) It is not necessary to treat this title much at length, as the subject is considered under other heads, especially CATTLE, and AGRICULTURE. The domesticated ox is met with in various parts of the world, and runs into as many varieties as the sheep; differing widely in size, form, and colour, according to climate and other... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 699]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
