      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "is the fermented juice of the grape. In the more southern states of Europe, the grapes, being more saccharine, afford a more abundant production of alcohol, and stronger wines, as exemplified in the best port, sherry, and madeira. The influence of solar heat upon the vines may, however, be mitigated by growing them to moderate heights on level ground, and by training them in festoons under the shelter of trees. In the more temperate climates, such as the district of... [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
