      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a choice edible fish frequenting the Northern seas and rivers, of which as much as 4000 tons' weight has sometimes been taken in a season, in the Irish and Scotch rivers, and tho greater part sent to London for sale. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 339]",
