      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the dried fruit of *Ficus carica*, chiefly imported from the Mediterranean ports. In 1855 we received upwards of 2200 tons, nearly all of which were for home consumption. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 164]",
