      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the fine soft short hair on the skin of some animals, which is worn for warmth or ornament; a scaly deposit, or calcareous incrustation in steam boilers, to prevent the accumulation of which a boiler compound is used; and a salinometer or gauge has been adopted for marine boilers. *See SALINOMETER.* [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 177]",
