      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_65_84_85_Textiles_Apparel_Footwear",
      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "The value of our silk manufactures exported has increased half-a-million every ten years since 1870. In 1889 it exceeded £2,780,000, including twist and yarn. In 1885 there were 691 silk factories in the United Kingdom, having 12,000 power-looms, 888,104 spinning spindles, and 174,644 doubling spindles. There were 42,990 persons employed in the silk factories. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 506]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
