      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Pomeranzen*. DU. *Oranjen*. DA. *Pomeranster*. SW. *Pomeranser*. FR. *Oranges*. IT. *Melarance*. SP. *Naranjas*. PORT. *Laranjas*. RUS. *Pomeranetzii*. POL. *Pomeranecz*. LAT. *Aurantia mala*.) This fruit is the produce of the *Citrus aurantium*, of which the varieties are, 1. Seville orange: this is a very handsome tree, and the hardiest of any; as in this country it shoots freely, produces large and beautiful leaves, flowers, &c. The fruit of this variety is large,... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 689]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
