      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Uhren*, *Taschenuhren*. Du. *Zakhorologien*, *Zaknurwerken*. DA. *Lommenhr*. Sw. *Fik-ur*, *Byxsüks-ur*. Fr. *Montres*. It. *Orinoli da tasca*, o *da sacoccia*. Sr. *Relojes de falriquera*. PORT. *Relogios de algibeira*. Rus. *Karmannüe tschasü*,) are movements or machines for the measuring of time, having their motion regulated by a spiral spring. WATCH, *Striking*, one which, besides the common watch-work for measuring time, has a clock part for striking the hours,... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 990]",
