      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "The following new Customs duty is granted by the Customs and Inland Revenue Act of 1870 in lieu of that previously levied:— 'Perfumed spirits and Cologne water being mixed with any article, so that the degree of strength cannot be ascertained by Sikes' hydrometer, the gallon, 16*s.* 6*d.*' Tinctures and medicinal spirits may be warehoused upon drawback, by a licensed rectifier or compounder of spirits in any Customs or Excise warehouse, like British Liqueurs, under 13 sect. [J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1765]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
