      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_29_Crude_Animal_Vegetable_Materials",
      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Lack*, *Gummilack*. DU. *Lak*, *Gomlak*. DA. *Lack*, *Gummilak*. SW. *Lack*, *Gummilak*. FR. *Lacque*, *Gomme lacque*. IT. *Lacca Gommalacca*. SR. *Goma lacca*. PORT. *Laca*. RU. *Laka*, *Gummilak*. POL. *Laka*, *Gumalaka*, LAT. *Gummi lacca*,) is the product of the *coccus lacca*, an insect, which deposits its eggs on the branches of a tree called Bihar, in Assam, a country bordering on Thibet, and elsewhere in India. It appears designed for defending the eggs from... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 551]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
