          "@value": "old rope",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "hard salted beef supplied to ships; old and condemned pieces of rope and cordage, cut into short lengths, and used for making mats, swabs, and oakum &c.; a Chinese vessel, from the Malay \"ajong.\" [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 223]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "19th-century maritime trade heading: old tarred hemp rope and cordage cut up for oakum caulking and paper-making, not miscellaneous scrap.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
