      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the bibrate of soda. This salt is largely imported from India under the name of *thical*, and after purification forms the refined *borix* of commerce. It is chiefly used as a flux for metals, and a constituent of the glazes for porcelain. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 58]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
