          "@value": "sodium carbonate",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the alkali obtained from common salt, manufactured to the extent of from 100,000 to 120,000 tons a year. It is used instead of barilla for soap-making, as a substitute for pot and pearl ashes in glass-making, and for bleaching and cleansing cotton. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 363]",
