      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Kastanien*. DU. *Kastanien*, *Karstengen*. DA. and Sw. *Kastanier*. FR. *Chataignes*. IT. *Castagne*. SP. *Castanas*. PORT. *Castanhas*. RUS. *Kaschtanü*. POL. *Kasztany*. LAT. *Castanæ*,) the fruit of the chesnut-tree, which in France is used as a substitute for potatoes, and oftentimes for bread. Horse-chesnuts are the fruit of the wild chesnut-tree. Starch of very excellent quality has been lately made from horse-chesnuts by a very simple process, similar to that... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 217]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
