      "skos:altLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "lemon",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Limonen*. DU. *Limoenen*. - DA. *Limoner*. - SW. *Lemoner*. FR. *Lemons*, *Citrons*. IT. *Limoni*. SP. *Limones*. PORT. *Limões*. RUS. *Limoni*. POL. *Limoni*. LAT. *Citrea mala*,) the fruit of the lemon-tree, growing in great abundance in Spain and Portugal, whence we import them, packed in chests and boxes. The ports of Lisbon and Malaga are the principal shipping places of lemons; the shipping of fruit from these places commences about the middle of September, and... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 572]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
