      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "or _Cinnabar_, is a compound of mercury and sulphur in the proportion of 100 parts of the former to 16 of the latter, which occurs in nature as a common ore of quicksilver, and is prepared by the chemist as a pigment, under the name of Vermillion. [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
