      "oe:isAggregate": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "ornaments for the person, which form a large article of commerce in Eastern countries and Africa; they are of glass, coral, amber, caracolian, and other substances, and range from seed beads to a very large size. The home manufacture exceeds in value £20,000 to £30,000 a-year. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 43]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
