        "@value": "ground chalk washed in alum-water, to cleanse it from sand and other impurities, and dried in lumps; it is used as a polishing material, and for making putty and white-wash. A small delicate sea-fish, the *Mertangus vulgaris*. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 424]",
