      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_22_Oil_Seeds_and_Oleaginous_Fruits",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Schafmüllen*. Du. *Kuischboomzaad*. DA. and SW. *Agnus-Castus frö*. FR. *Petit poivre*. IT. *Semenza d'agnocasto*. LAT. *Agni-Casti Semen*,) also called vitex seed, from the chaste tree. AGNATI, the relations by the father, who were preferred by the Roman laws to the cognati, or relations by the mother: till the edict of the emperor Justinian, Nov. 118, abolished all dis [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 30]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0124 (Oil & Essential Oil Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 30, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 438.",
