      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Bisamkörner*. Du. *Muskuszaad*. DA. *Desmerkorn*. Sw. *Desmanskorn*. IT. *Granelli d'ambretta*. SP. *Ambarilla*. PORT. *Ambaralhi*. POL. *Ziarnka pizmowe*. FR. *Ambrette*. LAT. *Abelmoschi grana*,) a small odoriferous seed used as a perfume. It is sometimes brought from Egypt, but is likewise imported from Martinico. AMBULANT, the name given at Amsterdam to brokers, or e [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 42]",
