      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "*Wall.*; *Fl. Br. Ind.*, ii., 450; Gamble, *Man. Ind. Timbs.*, 346; COMBRETACEÆ. The *dhaura*, *dhauri*, *dhavada*, *hesel*, *bákli*, *arma*, *vellay naga*, *chiriman*, etc. A large deciduous ## ANTIARIS TOXICARIA Upas Tree tree of the Sub-Himalayan tracts from the Ravi eastward to Central and Southern India. Ascends to 3,000 feet in altitude. Dhaura GUM is used in calico-print [Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 82]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0054 (Dye Stuffs & Dye Woods Unenumerated). Attested in: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 82.",
