      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an odoriferous gum-resin, obtained in Siam, and the Eastern Archipelago, from *Styrax Benzoin*, and used in perfume and license. It is of a yellowish gold colour with occasionally white almond-like masses in it; there are, however, two or three varieties which enter into commerce. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 46]",
