      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the leaf of the *Piper betel*, an ingredient of the betel masticatory, known as Pan in the East, where it forms nearly as extensive an article of commerce as tobacco in the West. There are several species of this scandent plant, which flourishes best in the islands of the Indian archipelago, furnishing leaves fit for use the second year, and continuing to yield them for more th [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 47]",
