      "oe:landBasis": "mineral",
      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_51_52_Chemicals",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a beautiful crystalline salt in large prisms, of a brilliant red color, used in dyeing and calico printing, obtained from chromate of iron, and which is the source of the chrome pigments. Mixed with sulphuric acid, it is a powerful oxidizing agent for bleaching oils and fats. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 48]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0506 (Chemical Manufactures and Products Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 48.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
