        "@value": "a reddish-white metal, occurring in brilliant plates, obtained chiefly in Saxony, and used as an alloy in type-metal and pewter. It is sometimes called by workmen tin-glass. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 50]",
