      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the flowers of *Anthemis nobilis*, in Europe are employed medicinally as a cheap tonic carminative andodyne; when taken in large doses, however, they prove powerfully emetic. Another species, *A. Pyrethrum* furnishes the pellitory root. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 76]",
