      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "*Guinea pepper*, is of three sorts, viz. 1. *Capsicum annuum*, the common long-podded capsicum. 2. *Capsicum baccacum*, the bird-pepper, grows nearly five feet high; the leaves are of a lucid green. This is the Cayenne-pepper. 3. *Capsicum grossum*, the bell-pepper. The fruit of this is red, and is the only kind proper for pickling, the skin being tender, whereas those of the o [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 200]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
