      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Akajuniisse*, *Westindische Anakarden*. DU. *Catsjoenooten*. DA. *Akajunvitter*. SW. *Akajunvitter*. FR. *Noix d'acajou*. IT. *Acaju*. SP. *Nueces d'acaju*. PORT. *Nozes d'acaju*.) The tree which yields these nuts grows naturally in the West Indies, and arrives at the height of 20 feet in those places of which it is a native. The fruit is as large as an orange; and is fu [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 207]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0012 (Seeds, Nuts & Kernels for Oil Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 207.",
