      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the small berry of *Anamirta paniculata*, and other species, imported from the East. From the bitter principle which they yield, these berries are said to be used to adulterate beer. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 108]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
