      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "COLOQUINTIDA, or BITTER CUCUMBER (Ger. koloquinten, coloquinten apfel; Dutch, bitter-appelen; Fr. coloquintes; Ital. coloquintida; Span. coloquintidas; Arab. and Pers. Hunzil). The produce of an annual plant (*Cucumis colocynthis*, Linn.; Nat. Order *Cucurbitaceæ*) growing in Turkey, Nubia, India, and other places, much resembling the cucumber in herbage. When ripe, the fruit i [J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 410]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 410, Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 233.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
