      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Englisches pflaster*. DU. *Engelsch pleister*. DA. *Engelskt plaster*. SW. *Engelskt pläster*. FR. *Taffetas d'Angleterre*. IT. *Taffeta d'Inghilterra*. SR. *Tafetan embalsamado de Inglaterra*. PORT. *Tafeta de Inglaterra*. LAT. *Emplastrum Anglicanum glutinans*,) a glutinous salve laid on fine black silk, and used as a healing plaster for slight sores. [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 255]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
