      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a grey or blackish variety of corundum, used to polish hard bodies. The powder is prepared by sieves, &c., from the size of pepper-corns to superfine flour, or impalpable dust. It is stuck on paper, cloth, and sticks. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 152]",
