      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the short soft silky white fur forming the winter clothing of the stoat, *Mustela erminea*; which is sought for extensively over northern Europe and America. It is worn by the judges, and for articles of ladies' dress. The black tuft from the tail is sewed to the skin at regular intervals. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 155]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0071 (Furs, Skins & Marine Products Unenumerated). Attested in: 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 155.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
