      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an umbelliferous plant, the *Anethum fœniculum dulce*, cultivated on the Continent as a pot-herb, and for the seeds and essential oil obtained from them. The seed is used in the manufacture of gin, and in medicine as a carminative. Another species, the common fennel, *Fœniculum officinale*, is cultivated in gardens as a garnish for fish, &c., and as a pot-herb for flavouring sa [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 162]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
