      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a name for the *Mustela Canadensis*; the skin is principally used for trimmings and linings, the fur being long, fine, and lustrous, but not so valuable as the sable. The tail is extensively used by the Jews. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 166]",
