      "oe:landBasis": "terrestrial_forest",
      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_29_Crude_Animal_Vegetable_Materials",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "Frankincense is an aromatic resin obtained from trees in the Burseracae family. (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankincense) The only entry for frankincense comes from the Pharmacopeia, which includes frankincense in the mixture for a Pitch Plaster. This frankincense is taken from resin cultivated in North America, produced from turpentine of Pinus Taeda. [Danika Drugs Project: British Pharmacopoeia (1867) / Savory (1865)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0220 (Gum, Resin & Elastic-Gum Unenumerated). Attested in: Danika Drugs.xlsx (British Pharmacopoeia 1867 / Savory 1865), 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 174, Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 439.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
