      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Walkererde*. DU. *Volluarde*. DA. *Walkejorde*. SW. *Valklera*, *Valkjord*. FR. *Terre à foulon*. IT. *Terra da purgatori*. SP. *Tierra de batan*. PORT. *Greda de pizoeiro*. RUS. *Schiffernaia glina*. LAT. *Terra fullonum*,) a species of clay, of a greyish ash-coloured brown, in all degrees from very pale to almost black, and it has generally something of a greenish cast [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 441]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0506 (Chemical Manufactures and Products Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 441, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 176.",
