      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "is a gum-resin, which occurs sometimes in yellow, shining tears, easily agglutinated; of a strong durable smell; an acrid and bitter taste; at other times in lumps. [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0220 (Gum, Resin & Elastic-Gum Unenumerated). Attested in: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 179.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562"
