      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_51_52_Chemicals",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a peculiar acid obtained from nut-galls, divi divi, and other vegetable substances, rich in tannin. It is used in photography and as a test to detect iron; and is well known as an ingredient of black dye and ink. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 179]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
