      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_54_Medicinal_Pharmaceutical",
      "skos:altLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "arapichea ipecacuanha",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "Ipecacuanha is a member of the flowering plant of the Rubiaceae family, with its root being used for medicinal purposes. (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carapichea_ipecacuanha) Ipecacuanha is a power full emetic (enduces vomiting) and was commonly used to treat cases of poisoning. It is also an expectorant (removes secretions from the lungs) and was also used in the treatment of those suffering from colds, coughs, ast [Danika Drugs Project: British Pharmacopoeia (1867) / Savory (1865)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: Danika Drugs.xlsx (British Pharmacopoeia 1867 / Savory 1865), Danika Drugs.xlsx (SKOS Sheet), 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab), Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 541. Research note: So much entries :S.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n541"
        }
      ]
    },
