      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "*Linn.*; *Fl. Br. Ind.*, v., 382-4; Gamble, *Man. Ind. Timbs.*, 1902, 612-3; Talbot, *List. Trees, etc.*, 1902, 309-10; Prain, *Beng. Plants*, 1903, ii., 941; Brandis, *Ind. Trees*, 1906, 576; EUPHORBIACEÆ. A genus of woody plants, chiefly natives of America. Four species are indigenous to India and three others naturalised or cultivated. **J. Curcas**, *Linn.*; *Rec. Bot. Surv [Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 711]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0012 (Seeds, Nuts & Kernels for Oil Unenumerated). Attested in: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 711.",
