      "skos:altLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "juniper berry",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "This entry deals with the Juniper berries, and how they were used in medicine. Although the Pharmacopeia includes an entry for Savin Tops (the fresh and dried tops of Juniperus Sabina, they have not been included). Juniper berries were used as a diuretic (increasing the secretion of urine), but could also be used as a stomachic, carminative, and diaphoretic. [Danika Drugs Project: British Pharmacopoeia (1867) / Savory (1865)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: Danika Drugs.xlsx (British Pharmacopoeia 1867 / Savory 1865), 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 476.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
