      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the brown seed of the *Sterculia acuminata*, about the size of a pigeon's egg, which are very highly esteemed in Africa. When chewed or sucked, they are said to enhance the flavour of any thing eaten afterwards, and also to purify putrid water. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 229]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
