      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. and DU. *Luzerne*. DA. and SW. *Luzerne*. FR. *Luzerne*. IT. *Lucerna*, *Erba spagna*. SP. *Alfalfa*. PORT. *Luzerna*, *Herva medica*. LAT. *Medicago*, *sativa*.) This seed produces a species of grass of very quick growth, which affords excellent fodder for cattle. It is a plant frequently cultivated in the manner of clover. Its leaves, like those of the latter, grow thre [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 605]",
