      "oe:groundingStatus": "document_attested_local",
      "oe:ghostAcresDomain": "fibres_textiles",
      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "*Cav.*; *Fl. Br. Ind.*, ii., 614-6; Duthie, *Fl. Upper Gang. Plain*, 1903, 367; Cooke, *Fl. Pres. Bomb.*, 1903, i., 531-3; Prain, *Beng. Plants*, 1903, i., 519-20; CUCURBITACEÆ. A genus of climbing plants, native of the warmer regions of the Old World and one indigenous in America. Four or five are wild in India. *L. acutangula*, Roxb.; Duthie and Fuller, *Field and Garden Crop [Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 766]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0822 (Vegetable Fibres Unenumerated (incl. Esparto, Cordage & Brush Fibres)). Attested in: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 766.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
