      "oe:groundingStatus": "document_attested_grounded",
      "oe:ghostAcresDomain": "tannins_leather",
      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the skin of this animal is of a greyish white, with dark spots. Being very soft, warm, and light, it is much used by the Chinese, Greeks, Persians, and others, for cloaks, linings, felts, &c. When dyed and prepared, the skins of the lynx and lynx cat, are exported in large numbers to the United States. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 247]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0071 (Furs, Skins & Marine Products Unenumerated). Attested in: 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 247.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
