      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a tropical fruit, the produce of trees of the *Mangifera* family, of which there are many cultivated varieties, although only two distinct species of tree. The fruit of the finer kinds have a rich perfumed grateful flavour; while others are so stringy and unpleasant as not to be eatable. The fruit is pickled and preserved, and made into a cloutney. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 250]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0408 (Spices Unenumerated (incl. Condiments & Minor Foods)). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 250.",
