      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_03_Fish_and_Seafood",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a small fish eight or nine inches in length and two in depth, the *Polynemus longifilis* of Cuvier, the *P. paradisus* of Linnaeus, esteemed as a delicacy in India, where it is also called the Tupsee. Isinglass is made of the swimming-bladder. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 250]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
