      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. DA. and Sw. *Mastix*. DU. *Mastik*. FR. *Mastic*. IT. *Mastice*. SP. *Almastica, Almacega*. PORT. *Almacega*. RUS. *Mastika*. POL. *Mastyks*. LAT. *Resina lentisina*.) The lesser turpentine-tree, and the *lentsicus*, afford the mastic of commerce. *See LENTISCK and GUM.* It is used in fumigations, in the composition of varnishes, and is supposed to strengthen the gums. Th [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 627]",
