      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a common name for several species of small seed corn. In the Mediterranean the millets are generally called Dhurra. On the Western African coast the chief millets grown are *Holcus lanatus*, *mollus*, and *spicatus*. In the West Indies millet passes under the name of Guinea corn. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 260]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0012 (Seeds, Nuts & Kernels for Oil Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 260, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854, Project Gutenberg #15191).",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
        {
