      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the seeds of *Abelmoschus moschatus*, of Wight and Arnott; the *Hibiscus abelmoschus* of Linnæus, which are stimulating, cordial, and stomachic, and made into a tincture by the Arabs, against serpent bites. See ABELMOSCHUS. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 267]",
