      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(**GER.** *Napelgelb*, *Neapolitanisch gelb*. **DU.** *Napels geel*. **DA.** and **SW.** *Neapelgult*. **FR.** *Jaune de Naples*. **IT.** *Giallolino*. **SP.** *Amarillo de Napoles*. **PORT.** *Amarelo de Napoles*. **RUS.** *Spelt Neapolitanskaja*.) According to Professor Beckmann, this colour is prepared by calcining lead with antimony and potash in a reverboratory furnace. Th [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 654]",
