      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_67_68_Metals",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a durable white metal easily malleable, resembling silver, usually procured from speise, a compound of the metal with arsenic, found associated with cobalt in Germany. Nickel is used to a very large extent in the arts, being remarkable for the peculiar whiteness and silver-like lustre which it communicates to other metals when alloyed with them. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 271]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
