        {
          "@value": "spirit of niter",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "spirit of nitre",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "Nitric acid is also know as the spirit of nitre (as such some treatments may have been included in Nitratine). It is a strong mineral acid that is highly corrosive. (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nitric_acid) Nitric acid was included in many solution in the Pharmacopeia, and is also included in test solutions that were used to verify the purity or inclusion of other materials. It was used in the Compendium as an astr [Danika Drugs Project: British Pharmacopoeia (1867) / Savory (1865)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0506 (Chemical Manufactures and Products Unenumerated). Attested in: Danika Drugs.xlsx (British Pharmacopoeia 1867 / Savory 1865), 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 272. Research note: lots entries.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n272"
        }
      ],
      "skos:closeMatch": [
