      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an oleo-resin obtained from the *Amyris Gileadensis*, and *A. Opobalsam*, which has a fragrant odour, and is used medicinally. It is sometimes called balm of Gilead, and is chiefly used as a cosmetic by the Turkish ladies. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 278]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
