      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an acrid medicinal gum-resin, obtained from the juice of the roots of *Opoponax Chironium*, in the Levant. In most of its properties it closely resembles asafoetida. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 278]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0220 (Gum, Resin & Elastic-Gum Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 278, Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 689.",
        "@language": "en"
