        "@value": "ORCHELLA, or ARCHELLA. (GER. *Orseille*. DU. *Orseille*, *Orcel*, *Orchillie*. DA. *Orselje*, *Furvemos*. SW. *Orsujä*. FR. *Orseille*. IT. *Oricello*, *Orcella*, *Rocella*, *Raspa*, *Rospo*, *Respio*. SP. *Orchilla*. PORT. *Orsella*, *Orzella*. RUS. *Arsel*. POL. *Mech farbierski*. LAT. *Rocella*.) The lichen *rocella*, or *orchella* weed, is a whitish moss, yielding a rich pu [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 690]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 690, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854, Project Gutenberg #15191).",
