      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(Eng. and Fr., _Yellow sulphuret of arsenic_; _Operment_, _Rauschgelb_, Germ.); occurs in indistinct crystalline particles, and sometimes in oblique rhomboidal prisms; but for the most part, in kidney and other imitative forms; it has a scaly and granular aspect; texture foliated, or radiated; fracture small granular, passing into conchoidal; splintery, opaque, shining, with a  [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
