      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an American term for a note or draft that is given in payment of an indebtedness, or for the purpose of raising money, and hence divided into \"business paper,\" which is given as payment for an actual indebtedness; and \"accommodation paper,\" given for the purpose of raising money and not for an indebtedness, which is made payable to the order of a person who consents to act as t [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 491]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0010 (Other Articles). Attested in: 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 491, Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 725. Research note: Too processed?.",
