        "@value": "(GER. *Amerikanische Grieswurzels*. DU. *Graveelwortel*. DA. *Amerikansk grususrod*. SW. *Grusrot*. FR. and IT. *Pareira-brava*. SP. *Parreira-brava*, *Butua*. PORT. and LAT. *Pareira brava*.) a hard, woody, crooked root, of a dark colour on the outside, and marked with various wrinkles, which run longitudinally and circularly. Its internal substance is of a dull yellowish colo [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 732]",
