      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a common name for sulphate of lime or gypsum, from its occurrence in the Paris formation. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 303]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0506 (Chemical Manufactures and Products Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 303, Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 763.",
