      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_53_Dyeing_Tanning_Colouring",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "The bark of a species of oak growing in many parts of North America. It is used in dyeing yellow colours. [BARK.] QUILLS (Fr. plumes à écrire; Ger. posen, federn, kiele; Ital. penna da scrivere; Russ. stivoli; Span. cañones para escribir). The hard and strong feather of the wings of geese, ostriches, swans, turkeys, crows &c. used in writing. They are classified according to th [J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1270]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0054 (Dye Stuffs & Dye Woods Unenumerated). Attested in: J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1270.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n1270"
        }
      ]
