      "oe:ghostAcresDomain": "drugs_botanicals_chemicals",
      "oe:landBasis": "terrestrial_crop",
      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_54_Medicinal_Pharmaceutical",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a valuable alkaloid, extracted from Cinchona bark, and used as a stimulant and tonic in intermittents. The sulphate of quinine is used to a great extent in medicine, for a medicinal wine, and in other forms. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 322]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: Danika Drugs.xlsx (British Pharmacopoeia 1867 / Savory 1865), Danika Drugs.xlsx (SKOS Sheet), 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 322. Research note: Quinia has entries too.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
