      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "*Linn.*; *Fl. Br. Ind.*, v., 457; EUPHORBIACEÆ. The Castor-oil Plant, Palma Christi, Ricin de Palma Christi, arand, erand, rand, bherenda, bindi, eri, areta, orer, rak-lop, anrar, gaba or jara, grundi, nerinda, rendi, harnauli, bazanjir, héran, ind, rund, amanakkam, kottei, amadan, amdi, haralu, kesu, kyetsu, etc. These vernacular names are mostly derived from the Sanskrit *era [Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 927]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0012 (Seeds, Nuts & Kernels for Oil Unenumerated). Attested in: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 927.",
