        "@value": "an alkaloid; the crystalline bitter principle of the bark of the willow, which is used medicinally as a febrifuge. Besides what is made at home, we imported, in 1855, 646 oz. [shrimp. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 338]",
