      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "*Schult., f.*; *S. zeylanica*, Roxb., *Fl. Ind.*, ii., 161; *Fl. Br. Ind.*, vi., 271; HÆMODORACEÆ. The Bowstring Hemp, *marûl*, *murva*, *murga*, *murgali*, *gorachakra*, *chaga*, etc., the Sanskrit for it being apparently *marura* (Jones, *As. Res.*, iv., 271). D.E.P., vi., pt. ii., 460-1. Bowstring Hemp. A stemless bush with a rosette of succulent radical leaves, each ending  [Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 987]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
