      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Sapanholz, Japanholz.* DU. *Sapanhout.* DA. *Sapanholt.* SW. *Sapan.* FR. *Bois de Sapan.* IT. *Legno di Sapan.* SR. and PORT. *Sapan.* LAT. *Lig-* *num Sappan,*) a species of wood, similar in every respect to the Brazil-wood, and employed for the same purposes. The tree, which produces it, is found in South America, Japan, and Cochin-china. The Sapan, and the cypress-tr [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 893]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0054 (Dye Stuffs & Dye Woods Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 893.",
