      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_24_Cork_and_Wood",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the wood and roots of the *Sassafras officinale*, a native of North America, which are brought over in billets. They are highly aromatic both in smell and taste. The dried leaves contain so much mucilage that they are used for thickening soups. \\* [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 341]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
