      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "*Fl. Br. Ind.*, iv., 387; Heuzé, *Les Pl. Indust.*, 1893, ii., 142-50; Semler, *Trop. Agrik.*, 1900, ii., 472-84; Wiesner, *Die Rohst. des Pflanzenr.*, 1903, ii., 768-78; PEDALINEÆ. Gingelly (or Gingeli) or Sesame Oil, *til*, *tir*, *tal*, *krishna*- or *kala-tél*, *rasí*, *sumsum* or *sim-sim*, *khasa*, *tilmin*, *míthá-tél*, *bhunguru*, *kunjad*, *kala katwa* (black), *purbia [Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 993]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0012 (Seeds, Nuts & Kernels for Oil Unenumerated). Attested in: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 993.",
