      "oe:ghostAcresDomain": "drugs_botanicals_chemicals",
      "oe:landBasis": "terrestrial_crop",
      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_54_Medicinal_Pharmaceutical",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Sucotrinaloe*. DU. *Sucotrinaloe*. DA. and SW. *Sokotrinaloe*. FR. *Aloes succotrin*, ou *chicotin*. IT. *Aloe succotrina*. SR. *Acibar cicotrina*. PORT. *Azevre succotrina*. LAT. *Aloe succotrina*.) See ALOES. SODA, is an alkaline salt, principally obtained from the ashes of marine plants. For this purpose considerable quantities of sea-weeds are collected on the coasts [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 936]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 936, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 507.",
