      "oe:landBasis": "mineral",
      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_51_52_Chemicals",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an incorrect name generally applied to a common effervescing beverage. The effervescent quality is not due to soda, but is produced by carbonic acid gas, which is forced into the water by an apparatus. The gas is produced by pouring sulphuric acid upon marble dust, or upon the super-carbonate of soda. The quantity of this cooling beverage made is very large, and with lemonade h [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 363]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 363, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 507.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n363"
