      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a name for the *Urginea Scilla* of Steinhell, the *Scilla maritima* of Linnaeus; a plant inhabiting the sea-coast of the Mediterranean, the acrid bulbs of which being diuretic, expectorant, emetic, and purgative, are used medicinally. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 369]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 369, Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 940.",
