      "oe:ghostAcresDomain": "drugs_botanicals_chemicals",
      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "*Dryand*; *Fl. Br. Ind.*, iii., 589; Gamble, *Man. Man. Ind. Timbs.*, 1902, 466; Brandis, *Ind. Trees*, 1906, 442; STYRACEÆ. The Benzoin Tree. The Resin = *lubán* (Ind. bazárs), *hussí*, *shambiráni*, *kaminian*, etc. A small tree of the Malay Archipelago, important as yielding the true Benzoin or Gum Benjamin of commerce. This substance appears to have been first mentioned by  [Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 1064]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 1064.",
