      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Takamahak*, *Hack und tack*. DU. *Takamahak*. DA. *Hak og tak*. SW. *Tacamahac*. FR. *Tacamacha*, *Gomme tamacha*. IT. *Taccamaca*. SP. and PORT. *Tacamaca*. LAT. *Tacamahaca*,) a solid resinous substance brought from New Spain; it is said to be collected likewise in certain other provinces of America, and in the island of Madagascar. There are two sorts of it. The best  [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 954]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0220 (Gum, Resin & Elastic-Gum Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 954, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 382.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
