      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a name for the common vetch, *Vicia sativa*, a generally cultivated fodder plant; the seed is also used for feeding poultry. Of this seed the average annual imports from abroad, in the three years ending with 1856, were about 29,000 quarters. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 385]",
