      "oe:landBasis": "terrestrial_crop",
      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_05_Vegetables_and_Fruit",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the fruit or seed contained in the capsules of *Depteryx odorata*, principally used to impart fragrance to snuff. See **CAMARA**. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 396]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0012 (Seeds, Nuts & Kernels for Oil Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 396.",
