      "oe:landBasis": "terrestrial_crop",
      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_07_Coffee_Tea_Cocoa_Spices",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a pungent blistering liquor, extracted from the vesicatory beetle: a piece of blotting paper soaked in it makes a ready blister. *See CANTHARIDES.* [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 414]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 414.",
