      "oe:landBasis": "mineral",
      "oe:sitcCode": "SITC4_51_52_Chemicals",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "OIL OF: *see* **SULPHURIC ACID**. **VIVRES** (French), provisions, food, diet. **VLOCK**, a Polish land measure, equal to 4148 acres. **VOBLA**, a name in Greece for the *Leuciscus rutilus*. **VODE**, a woollen fabric for religious uses. **VOĐKA**, a vile rye whiskey made in Russia, but the term generally means a dram of spirits. **VOODOVICK**, a decked boat in Russia. **VOG**, [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 518]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0506 (Chemical Manufactures and Products Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 518, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 414.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
