      },
      "oe:groundingStatus": "document_attested_local",
      "oe:ghostAcresDomain": "drugs_botanicals_chemicals",
      "oe:landBasis": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "There are numerous entries under volatile in the Pharmacopeia and Compendium, and while the volatile listed in the import/export data is liquid ammonia, the distinction is not made clear in the medical texts. This entry contains information on item listed under volatile, sal volatile, or any liquid form of ammonia. Ammonia was included in a large assortment of remedies in the Pharmacopeia, and in the Compendium it wa [Danika Drugs Project: British Pharmacopoeia (1867) / Savory (1865)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: Danika Drugs.xlsx (British Pharmacopoeia 1867 / Savory 1865), 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab). Research note: Liquid ammonia. Has entried in CDM under volatile. Pharm: have to look for it directly, ammonia has a lot of entries but nothing under volatile. Sal volatile..",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    },
